"""Write extraction evidence from immutable capture and explicit recipes."""
import importlib.util,json
from pathlib import Path
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('slope',HERE.with_suffix('.py'));g=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(g)
qs=g.SOURCE['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']
family={
'double_sin':'x=a sin(2t), y=b sin²(t): power/chain derivatives, double-angle identity, half-tangent evaluation.',
'double_cos':'x=a sin(2t), y=b cos²(t): negative power/chain derivative, double-angle identity, half-tangent evaluation.',
'poly5':'x=a t²+c, y=b t⁵+t³: two power-rule terms, factor a quadratic in t², cancel t, evaluate.',
'trig_poly':'x=a sin(t), y=(b/π)t²: basic trig and power derivatives, secant quotient, exact angle and π cancellation.',
'cubic':'x=t³+a t², y=b t²: polynomial derivatives, cancellation of a common t, rational slope.',
'linear_trig':'x=a t+sin(t), y=b t+cos(t): additive linear/trig derivatives; evaluate exact sine/cosine values.',
'poly4':'x=a t³+1, y=b t⁴+c t²: two power-rule terms, factor/cancel t; rational slope.',
'harmonic':'x=a cos(t), y=b sin(nt), n=2 or 3: retain frequency from chain rule; evaluate different exact angles.',
'ellipse':'x=a sin(t), y=b cos(t): basic derivatives and signed scaled tangent at a standard angle.',
'exp_root':'x=1/(a√t), y=eᵗ/(bt): negative half-power and quotient derivatives; cancel t powers and evaluate exponential/root.',
'reciprocal_exp_root':'x=e^(a/t), y=b/√(t²+c): two chain derivatives, cancel negative signs, evaluate fractional exponent and root powers.',
'nested_trig':'x=a√sin(eᵗ), y=b cot(eᵗ): nested root/trig/exponential chains; cancel common eᵗ and evaluate e^(ln θ).',
}
lines=['# Classification','Database `math`, basis **1356**, lineage `'+g.SOURCE['lineage']+'`. All 18 practice questions classified; canonical e-596 is context only.','| Level | Field layouts | Templates | Sources | Plot rating |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|','| easy | 7 radio templates (5 choices), 1 blank (`m=`; one answer fragment) | 8 | 8 | light: cubic radio/blank |','| moderate | 1 radio, 2 blank templates | 3 | 4 | moderate: all include curve plot |','| hard | 3 radio, 2 blank templates | 5 | 6 | none |','## Complete source assignment','| Source | Difficulty | Template | Bank profile | Parameters |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
for q in qs:
 qid=q[':question/math-academy-id'];t=g.SOURCE_TEMPLATE[qid];v=g.TEMPLATES[t]
 lines.append('| '+qid+' | '+v[0]+' | '+t+' | '+('observed_'+qid if v[1]=='radio' else 'blank: no distractors')+' | `'+json.dumps(g.PARAMETERS[qid])+'` |')
lines+=['## Curriculum scope','Followed `activity/first-step` → `step/next`: introduction (17592186084147), parametric derivative sibling (17592186084148), slope KP (17592186084152). The prerequisite formula is y′(t)/x′(t). Canonical e-596 evaluates a product/exponential derivative at t=1. Sources anchor every generated level; no missing-level authorship is needed. Frequencies two/three, inverse roots/exponentials, nested chains, field layouts and finite slopes are all observed. Tangent equations, second derivatives and undefined-slope questions belong to other demands and are excluded.','## Fidelity limits and corrections','All complete radio profiles are retained, including uncertain numeric scalar patterns. They are explicit replay profiles rather than asserted recovered author algorithms. Normal radio banks are separately labeled authored operations. q-20991 and q-348305 display an invalid all-real interval for reciprocal √t; generated domains are corrected to t>0. Raw evidence is unchanged; these prompts cannot count as exact text matches. Equivalent standard LaTeX replaces source invisible function application and redundant braces. Normal blank presentation replaces “Do not round the answer.” with “Give an exact answer.” to avoid the native grader’s substring-triggered exact-form mode. Explicit profile="observed" retains the original sentence and its native capability limitation. No missing fields, unrated questions or omitted questions.']
(HERE/'classification.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
lines=['# Template extraction','Snapshot provenance: math / basis 1356 / lineage '+g.SOURCE['lineage']+'.','## Stage 1 — specific original descriptions']
for q in qs:
 qid=q[':question/math-academy-id'];t=g.SOURCE_TEMPLATE[qid];v=g.TEMPLATES[t];fld=q[':question/answer-fields'][0]
 lines+=['### '+qid,q[':question/problem'],'Original parameters: `'+json.dumps(g.PARAMETERS[qid])+'`. Exact input numbers are integers, rational multiples of π, or ln(π/6). Required slope is an exact rational, radical or exponential/radical value, with sign preserved. '+family[v[2]],'Field `'+fld[':answer-field/key']+'`, `'+fld[':answer-field/type'][':db/ident']+'`; expected fragment contains only the slope (not `m=` or a tangent equation). Original correct value: `$'+fld[':answer-field/correct'][':answer/value']+'$`. Plot role: '+('blue parametric curve on grid before the prompt' if v[4] else 'none')+'.']
lines+=['## Stage 2 — shared patterns','All questions supply t explicitly, differentiate both coordinate functions, form the quotient y′/x′, simplify, substitute the given t, and return one exact finite slope. They do not require recovering t from a coordinate point. Same parameters at different supplied t remain separate math instances.']
for f,desc in family.items():lines.append('- **'+f+'**: '+desc)
lines+=['## Stage 3 — every original choice and its complete bank','Each table maps one original field/choice to an explicit normal-generator expression recipe at the source parameters. Formula implementations are in `bank` in the sibling script. Scalar evidence alone underdetermines error intent. “Empirical” means expression-pattern preservation, not a recovered diagnosis; these banks are offered only through explicit observed profiles.']
for q in qs:
 qid=q[':question/math-academy-id'];t=g.SOURCE_TEMPLATE[qid];v=g.TEMPLATES[t];p=g.PARAMETERS[qid];d=g.mathematics(v[2],p)
 vals,recipes=g.bank(v[2],p,d,'observed_'+qid) if v[1]=='radio' else ([d['m']],['correct slope fragment'])
 lines+=['### '+qid+' / '+('observed_'+qid if v[1]=='radio' else 'blank'),'Parameters: `'+json.dumps(p)+'`.','| Source field | Complete source value | Correct? | Parameterized recipe / pattern | Generated exact value |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
 for option in q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/choices']:
  # Source bank order matches the recipe list here; generated option order is
  # independently shuffled. Math matching is proved by validate.py.
  i=q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/choices'].index(option)
  lines.append('| '+q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/key']+' | `$'+option[':answer/value']+'$` | '+str(option[':answer/id']==q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/correct'][':answer/id'])+' | '+recipes[i]+' | `$'+g.tex(vals[i])+'$` |')
lines+=['## Stage 4 — reusable Markdown/value templates','There are 16 observed field/value templates. Different numbers within a template do not count as another template. Blank harmonic n=2/n=3 cases share one layout; reciprocal exponential/root blanks with c=1/c=4 share another. Radio/blank prompt endings and field fragments remain distinct.','Fixed source wording: “For the parametric curve”; “shown above” iff plotted; “calculate the slope … of the tangent to the curve at the point where t=…”; blank source replay (API profile="observed") adds “Do not round the answer.” and `$m=$ {{field-1}}`. Normal blanks use “Give an exact answer.” as a minimal native-grading compatibility repair: the current grader treats any “round” substring as requiring normalized identical form, so even “Do not round” rejects a valid unreduced derivative quotient. The exact mathematical demand, field fragment, level and fixed solution are unchanged. Original-wording rejection evidence is separate from accepted algebraically equivalent normal entries. Worked solution retains “We will use the formula”, “Differentiating x and y, we get”, “So we have” (radio) / “So, we have” (blank), then “Therefore, when …”. Exactly one fixed worked solution is independent of option selection.','Variable components are x(t), y(t), interval, t₀, derivative factors, unreduced derivative quotient, simplified ratio, substitution, special-angle or exact numerator/denominator evaluation, final slope, and complete bank. Optional plots depend on the same curve parameters. Standard LaTeX and algebraically equivalent factorization normalize mathematical blocks; source text/math evidence remains in source.json and review.md. Exact raw source strings are reported separately from mathematical bank fidelity.','Sampling policies (authored, not recovered code): positive small coordinate coefficients a,b∈1..6; polynomial shifts −4..6; low positive secondary coefficients; integer t values of magnitude 1..4 (cubic includes signed t); standard exact trig angles within the original [0,2π) interval (linear/trig: π/2 or 3π/2; trig/polynomial: odd multiples of π/4; harmonic/ellipse: common multiples of π/6, π/4, π/3); harmonic n∈{2,3}; hard exponential/root t in 2..6; reciprocal-root c∈{−1,1,2,3,4} with positive radicand; nested eᵗ is π/6 or 5π/6, below e, preserving sin(eᵗ)=1/2 and the original half-power workload. All source parameters remain accepted with explicit replay profiles. Scope stays at the same derivative method and algebra size. There is no within-level progression.','Validation constraints: supplied parameter in displayed interval, both coordinate values real, x′(t₀)≠0, slope finite, and all required bank options real, finite, pairwise inequivalent, with exactly one correct. Choose the complete bank before sampling and reject the entire instance on any failure. Explicit parameter input fails rather than silently resampling. No coordinate-point ambiguity arises because t₀ is supplied.','Authored normal banks: slope; reversed derivative sign; reversed derivative ratio; omit division by x′; use y/x. The linear/trig template instead uses reverse cosine derivative sign, omit cosine derivative, leave y undifferentiated, and evaluate at half the supplied parameter, which supports the observed zero slope without a reciprocal-zero option. These are complete authored banks, never claims about original author intent. Instance eligibility rejects any collisions (including zero slopes for banks whose sign-reversal options collide).','Source correction: q-20991 and q-348305 have x=1/(a√t), y=eᵗ/(at) yet −∞<t<∞. √t must be real and nonzero, so t>0. Evaluated source slopes remain correct and all source options replay. The generated interval alone is corrected.']
(HERE/'template-extraction.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
